commit b3326049f373cf16e85e9178f4c90b838e97ac6a

C03: the written file name is observed data and measures are written as observed (FILES1711)

In FILES1709 the drafts named the written file correctly and the code-shape veto rejected them because the name returned by filesystem.write.text was not among the observed names it exempts; the CPU variant could not ground its write because the CPU percentage was rendered with six significant digits. The name returned by a verified filesystem.write.text is now observed data for the veto, and every measure in the projected file is rendered exactly as the observation carries it (an integer, or the shortest round-trip of a float; an exponent form abstains).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


diff --git a/src/baxy_mind/__main__.py b/src/baxy_mind/__main__.py
index 8a497fc7..b3045e72 100644
--- a/src/baxy_mind/__main__.py
+++ b/src/baxy_mind/__main__.py
@@ -853,7 +853,16 @@ def _process_report_file_arguments(
             measure = entry.get("totalProcessorSeconds")
         if isinstance(measure, bool) or not isinstance(measure, (int, float)):
             return None
-        rendered = str(measure) if isinstance(measure, int) else format(measure, 'g')
+        # Rendered exactly as the observation JSON carries it (shortest
+        # round-trip for a float, no exponent), so the line stays evidence.
+        if isinstance(measure, int):
+            rendered = str(measure)
+        elif measure.is_integer():
+            rendered = str(int(measure))
+        else:
+            rendered = repr(measure)
+            if 'e' in rendered or 'E' in rendered:
+                return None
         lines.append(f"{entry['name'].strip()}: {rendered}")
     if not lines:
         return None
